@page "/"

<PageTitle>FronteggAuth Blazor sample</PageTitle>

<h1>You are signed in</h1>

<p>
    Reaching this page means the whole interactive flow worked: the package's gating middleware saw an
    unauthenticated browser request, challenged the <code>Frontegg.Oidc</code> scheme, Frontegg authenticated
    you, and the callback wrote the session cookie.
</p>

<p>Two pages show what the package puts in front of a Blazor component:</p>

<ul>
    <li>
        <a href="user">Current user</a> — the <code>ApplicationUser</code> projection, statically
        server-rendered so it can read the request principal.
    </li>
    <li>
        <a href="reports">Reports</a> — gated by
        <code>[Authorize(Policy = "perm:sample.reports.read")]</code>. Without that permission in your tenant
        you get the <em>Not authorized</em> message rather than a redirect.
    </li>
</ul>
